From: Ayushman Chhabra <14110965+ayushmanchhabra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:57:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix crash when picking a folder with nwdirectory

<input nwdirectory> picks the folder itself, so base_dir is empty, and
RemoveSymlinks() CHECKs that it isn't (fatal since Chromium 154). Pass
such selections on without filtering.

Refs: nwjs/nw.js#8393
---
 content/browser/web_contents/file_chooser_impl.cc | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/content/browser/web_contents/file_chooser_impl.cc b/content/browser/web_contents/file_chooser_impl.cc
index d0e46983..8361972d 100644
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/file_chooser_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/file_chooser_impl.cc
@@ -102,7 +102,14 @@ void FileChooserImpl::FileSelectListenerImpl::FileSelected(
   if (!owner_)
     return;
 
-  if (mode != blink::mojom::FileChooserParams::Mode::kUploadFolder) {
+  // NW.js: an <input nwdirectory> picks the folder itself instead of
+  // uploading its contents (FileSelectHelper's !extract_directory_), so there
+  // is no `base_dir` and nothing enumerated in it for RemoveSymlinks() to
+  // filter; RemoveSymlinks() CHECKs `base_dir` isn't empty
+  // (nwjs/nw.js#8393). The renderer gets the empty `base_dir` as before, so
+  // the folder has no relative path.
+  if (mode != blink::mojom::FileChooserParams::Mode::kUploadFolder ||
+      base_dir.empty()) {
     owner_->FileSelected(base_dir, mode, std::move(files));
     return;
   }
